      "id": "rc:4003624060",
      "kind": "approach",
      "harm": "retaining block stats from before a failed mempool reload can allow an unready mempool to pass health checks and return inaccurate fee estimates",
      "quote": "I still find myself thinking we should clear the whole mined-block window when the mempool does not reload. Those observations measured _the mempool we lost_, while the health check is meant to tell us whether the _current mempool matches mined blocks_.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "author_replies": [
        "rc:4008918858"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": true,
      "settled_by_id": "rc:4008918858",
      "settled_by_quote": "I pushed both in the new push, clearing the stats and also having a warm-up time where we suspect the mempool is sparse because the node has not run long enough."
    },
    {
      "id": "r:5208559358",
      "kind": "interface",
      "harm": "returning an error on LOW_COVERAGE rather than falling back to block policy leaves callers without an estimate despite block policy being valid",
      "quote": "Should `LOW_COVERAGE` also fall back to the block-policy estimate in combined mode? It tells us that we shouldn't use the **mempool** to lower the estimate, but doesn't necessarily invalidate the available block-policy estimate.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "author_replies": [
        "c:5682265146"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": true,
      "settled_by_id": "c:5682265146",
      "settled_by_quote": "Indeed, I force-pushed fb385bfaac...a623083db1 to fix that. The only exception that we return an error is when the mempool is still loading."
    },
    {
      "id": "rc:4021617875",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "harm": "persisting warmup end height could lead to incorrect warmup state across restarts with long downtime",
      "quote": "Why does this need to be persisted? In what case would it make sense for a warmup to start and get interrupted and then continue?",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "author_replies": [
        "rc:4036669492",
        "rc:4037682824"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": true,
      "settled_by_id": "rc:4037682824",
      "settled_by_quote": "Pushed a fix, warmup now re-starts whenever the tracked mined-block window is empty"
    },
    {
      "id": "rc:4030465853",
      "kind": "interface",
      "harm": "failing to fall back to block policy while the mempool is still loading unnecessarily denies an estimate to callers",
      "quote": "I am slightly inclined to suggest for the sake of simplicity that whatever the error is, just fall back to block policy.",
      "blocking": false,
